<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oktoberfest</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1810</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oktoberfest is the annual folk festival held on the Theresienwiese in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>. It began with a horse race on 17 October 1810 celebrating the wedding of Crown Prince Ludwig of Bavaria and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/therese-of-saxe-hildburghausen">Therese of Saxe-Hildburghausen</a>, and became a yearly event. Now held from late September into early October, it is the largest festival of its kind in the world, known for its beer tents and parades.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oktoberfest.jpg" alt="Oktoberfest" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Heribert Pohl --- Thanks for half a million clicks! from Germering bei München, Bayern · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:O%27zapft_is!_M%C3%BCnchens_5_Jahreszeit_hat_begonnen_-_O%27zapft_is!_Munich_5_season,_the_Oktoberfest_has_begun_(9855483374).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
